//// log — levels, the log record, the four renderers, the one error digest and
//// a `Logger` whose sink is injected. A bundled library (decisions 194, 195),
//// neutral like `routing`: it imports `std` and nothing else, ships `.bp`
//// files only (decision 117 rule 8) and is compiled for erlang and commonJS
//// from one source, so a line and a digest read the same on both.
////
//// Consumers write `import {logging.Logger, digest.errorDigest} from "log";`
//// (decision 107). Moved from rakun-logging's pure half (`levels.bp`,
//// `formats.bp`, `digest.bp`, the `Logger`); its OTP cells stay rakun's, and
//// rakun installs them as the sink. See `../AGENTS.md`.
////
//// The `files` ORDER in `botopink.json` is a dependency order: a module is
//// listed before the siblings that import it.

pub mod levels;
pub mod formats;
pub mod digest;
pub mod sink;
pub mod logging;
